From 09f39fa1449a5b95deaba10b05355aff3b7ce876 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: albanread <albanread@googlemail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 10:32:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] boot loader: skip an unusable blocked entry, as packagefs
 does

The boot loader reads the system's packages settings with its own copy of
packagefs's PackageSettingsItem, and it had the bug patch 0142 fixed in
packagefs: an entry that AddEntry() refuses -- an empty name, as in
BlockedEntries { "" } -- left its out-parameter unset, and the loop marked
whatever the pointer held as blocked. In the EFI loader that fault stops
the machine before the kernel starts: one line in
/boot/system/settings/packages made the system unbootable.

Such an entry is skipped now, and only a memory shortage ends the parsing.

Test: HaikuArmQemu's tools/analysis-fixes/packagefs-boot-test.sh. With
BlockedEntries { "" bin/fortune } written, the next boot stopped in the
boot loader (Virtualization.framework: "Internal Virtualization error",
right after PackageVolumeInfo::SetTo()); now the system comes up with
bin/fortune blocked.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Prose-Patch: 0150-boot-loader-skip-an-unusable-blocked-entry-as-packagefs-does.patch 844baece3ac07c52e67a4dca1d46d5856ccee315f66c4fbe592646e100984efe
---
 .../file_systems/packagefs/PackageSettingsItem.cpp     | 10 +++++++---
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/system/boot/loader/file_systems/packagefs/PackageSettingsItem.cpp b/src/system/boot/loader/file_systems/packagefs/PackageSettingsItem.cpp
index 39934c0570..ddcdefdd27 100644
--- a/src/system/boot/loader/file_systems/packagefs/PackageSettingsItem.cpp
+++ b/src/system/boot/loader/file_systems/packagefs/PackageSettingsItem.cpp
@@ -173,9 +173,13 @@ PackageSettingsItem::_AddBlockedEntries(const driver_parameter& parameter)
 	for (int i = 0; i < parameter.parameter_count; i++) {
 		Entry* entry;
 		status_t error = AddEntry(parameter.parameters[i].name, entry);
-		// abort only in case of serious issues (memory shortage)
-		if (error == B_NO_MEMORY)
-			return error;
+		if (error != B_OK) {
+			// abort only in case of serious issues (memory shortage); skip
+			// anything else, such as an empty name, which leaves entry unset
+			if (error == B_NO_MEMORY)
+				return error;
+			continue;
+		}
 
 		entry->SetBlocked(true);
 	}
